{
  "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
  "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:23 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GEN. PAUL D. CLEMENT, ESQ., Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "CBOCS West, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Based on the plain terms of section 1981, this Court's interpretation of that statute under Runyon, Patterson, and Domino's Pizza, as well as Congress' recognition of the distinction between discrimination and retaliation and this Court's decision in Burlington Northern, section 1981 does not contain a separate cause of action for retaliation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you see any meaningful difference between the language of 1981 and 1982 in this regard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do have those recent cases, but we also have the Sullivan case interpreting -- interpreting 1982, which arose under the prior approach to these questions. And my question for you is: Under principles of stare decisis, which body do we follow, the earlier case interpreting 1982 under the more freewheeling approach to statutory interpretation or this later body of law that says we're not going to do that any more?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Hawkins, is it at all relevant on the issue that the several courts of appeals have come out the same way both before the 1991 amendment and since the 1991 amendment, and opinions to the contrary are pretty scarce? Does that have any weight in a sort of a stare decisis sense?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF CYNTHIA H. HYNDMAN ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Cynthia H. Hyndman",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner's basically asking this Court to allow an employer to be able to fire an employee who brought a private lawsuit to enforce his section 1981 rights. If the Court were to allow employers to do that, then any employer or contracting party would have the ability to exempt themselves from section 1981 liability. Take the example of a person who complains that he was not promoted because of his race in violation of section 1981. His employer fires him for making that complaint. If he did not have protection under section 1981 against retaliation, he would never have the opportunity to remedy that discriminatory promotion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Cynthia H. Hyndman",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 1981 doesn't provide any specific remedies or any type of enforcement mechanism. It can only be enforced through a private lawsuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You're saying they would have -- you're saying they would have added an express retaliation provision in 1981 in 1991 if they had thought that the mode of reasoning in Sullivan was no longer sound? Is that what this comes down to?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When you say they legislated against the backdrop, you're -- are you not relying on something they didn't do, rather than anything that they did?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Hyndman",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That's correct, Justice Ginsburg; and at that time this Court said that you look to the language of the statute, and there in Title IX the language was broad. It was a general ban on discrimination, such as we have in section 1981 and section 1982, and in fact the Jackson court relied on Sullivan and relied on this Court's interpretation of Sullivan to find that there was a cause of action for retaliation under Title IX."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is the Government going to be consistent in this position?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you asking us to infer, to find implied in the words a cause of action against retaliation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If we thought Sullivan was incorrectly decided, what should we do?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael W. Hawkins",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent and the government and its amicus arguments are more appropriate on the floor of Congress debating whether or not to amend section 1981 to include retaliation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e7104dd5442e-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is no longer Washington, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2007-06-1431",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "e7104dd5442e8ccbc547af4d11d1d077d8758de2fc2da7d35ef5926c0aa2766e",
